WEBVTT

00:00:00.229 --> 00:00:04.397
Open Calculators and create a private floor slab study.

00:00:04.397 --> 00:00:05.283
Set a six-metre, 300 mm deep bonded strip. The tendon area, eccentricity and effective force will also feed the resistance calculation.

00:00:05.283 --> 00:00:05.934
Declare one physical bonded tendon layer at midspan. Enter the concrete data and the concrete strain at effective prestress; tension is positive.

00:00:05.934 --> 00:00:14.836
Paste the strain and stress pairs from the tendon curve. Here the curve is synthetic and is used only for training. Explicitly choose no ordinary bars for the first comparison.

00:00:14.836 --> 00:00:20.345
The ultimate demand is 64.530 kNm. The neutral axis is 50 mm below the top, giving 266.690 kNm of design resistance before adding ordinary bars.

00:00:20.345 --> 00:00:28.262
With 300 mm² of 500N bars at 260 mm depth, design resistance becomes 286.973 kNm. Read the minimum nominal strength and ductility checks separately. Overall design approval remains with the engineer.

00:00:28.262 --> 00:00:33.399
Issue the saved revision in Project Summary. The report preserves the current demand, resistance and native calculation appendix.
